    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 271 of 2006",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A5939\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend chapter 271 of the laws of 2006, amending the environ-\nmental conservation law relating to adding areas of Ulster county within\nthe Catskill park to the Hudson river valley greenway, in relation to\nthe effectiveness of such chapter\n\nPURPOSE:\nRevives Chapter 271 of the Laws of 2006, relating to adding areas of\nUlster county within the Catskill Park to the Hudson River Valley Green-\nway and makes it permanent.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nAmends Section 3 of Chapter 271 of the Laws of 2006 amending the envi-\nronmental conservation law relating to adding areas of Ulster County\nwithin the Catskill Park to the Hudson River Valley Greenway by removing\nthe expiration date reviving the provisions of the law and deeming them\nin full force and effect as they existed on December 31, 2008.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\nUlster County communities located in the Catskill Park are no longer\neligible for membership in the Greenway since Chapter 271 of the Laws of\n2006 expired on January 1, 2009.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nHudson River Valley Greenway has been a successful program that assists\nmembership communities with natural and cultural resource protection,\nregional planning, economic development, public access and heritage\nenvironmental education. Chapter 271 of the Laws of 2006 granted Ulster\nCounty communities located in the Catskill Park the option of joining\nthe Greenway. This act expired on January 1, 2009. This bill revives\nChapter 271 of the Laws of 2006 and removes the expiration allowing\nthose communities the continued opportunity for membership in the Green-\nway.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2008 - A.11168 - Vetoed by Governor\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have been\nin full force and effect on and after December 31, 2008.\n\n",
